# CHANGELOG — ws-codeqlfix (CodeQL perf findings T-CODEQL-1..5)

Tree: `.swarm/ws-codeqlfix` (base commit a49f18d "workspace base"). Config:
`CONFIG_NATIVE_MODULES=y CONFIG_TLS=y`, `-j3`. Control: `dynajs.base`
(snapshotted before the first source edit). Baseline gates on the control:
dataframe 42456+152, mathx 356/308/418, ml 59/75/2414 (+343 selection),
html 108+9, string 51159+63 — all green BEFORE any change.

## T-CODEQL-1 — dataframe groupby-last ring `% cnt[g]` — KEPT

- Sites: `src/dyna-dataframe.c` pass-2 ring fill (`head[g]+1 % cnt[g]`) and
  unwrap (`(head[g]+j) % cnt[g]`, the cited line).
- Fix: conditional subtract / moving index. Equivalence is provable: the ring
  must hold EXACTLY cnt[g] arrivals (which rows survive), so power-of-two
  sizing + mask is NOT applicable (it would change which arrivals a window
  keeps); head[g] < cnt[g] and j < cnt[g] give a single-wrap bound.
- A/B (4-way variant matrix, interleaved, 5 reps, `probe/bench_df_last.js`,
  `scratch/ab_df_matrix.log`): dominant-group shape (3 groups, k=65536)
  18.96 -> 14.68 ms median (-22.6%), reproduced in two independent builds
  (fill-only v1 and both v3), 5/5 reps each. many-groups shape: 16.44 vs
  16.38 ms (neutral). k=1 shape: 13.49 vs 13.84 ms (+2.6%) — PROVEN layout
  artifact: v1-vs-v3 differ 0.43 ms on byte-identical C code for that shape,
  and v2-vs-base (+2.9%) also differs with identical code.
- Correctness: `probe/df_last_diff.js` differential vs a JS reference ring —
  487/487 on base AND fixed (group sizes straddling k, k=1, exact multiples,
  prime row counts, head on every residue class). Suites green post-change.

## T-CODEQL-2 — pad `% plen` per char — REVERTED (negative result)

- Audit correction first: the real `String.prototype.padStart/padEnd`
  (`js_string_pad`, string.inc.c:1228) is ALREADY modulo-free (chunked
  `string_buffer_concat`/`string_buffer_fill`, upstream QuickJS shape). The
  cited lines 2345/2348 are the DynaJS `pad()` EXTENSION (center-pad). The
  test262 surface was never touched; no test262 run needed.
- Tried two equivalent rewrites (wrap cursor under the `have_pad` ternary;
  then loops split on `have_pad`): 4.66 -> 4.75-4.77 ms on a 2e6-char pad
  (+2%, 12/12 then 9/9 reps, four pad shapes). The loop is
  `string_buffer_putc16`-bound; the per-char index math is not the cost.
- Reverted; `probe/pad_diff.js` (1620 asserts vs a repeat+slice reference,
  wide-char matrix) green on base and post-revert; string suites green.

## T-CODEQL-3 — mathx factor `x / d` per candidate — KEPT (2.00x)

- The cited loop pays TWO 64-bit divisions per odd candidate: the overflow-
  safe condition `d <= x / d` AND the factor test `x % d` (the sketch in the
  findings only promises removing the first). Fix: `limit = isqrt(x)`
  recomputed only after a factor shrinks x (<= 53 times), then
  `if (x % d == 0) do {...} while` — one division per candidate.
- `d <= isqrt(x) <=> d*d <= x <=> d <= x/d` (floor) — exact, including the
  d*d == x boundary. isqrt via sqrtl + correction loops (r <= 2^27 in the
  <= 2^53 domain, no overflow).
- A/B x3 interleaved (`probe/bench_factor.js`, worst cases: p*p at the
  d*d==x boundary, prime near 2^53): 58.9 -> 29.4 ms median on EVERY input,
  12/12 reps.
- Correctness: `probe/factor_diff.js` — exhaustive [1, 200000] vs an
  independent BigInt reference PLUS adversarial big values (semiprime
  squares, primes near 2^53, prime powers) verified by product + ascending +
  deterministic Miller-Rabin: 200037/200037 identical on base and fixed.
  (First draft of the probe's own MR powmod was wrong — fixed the probe, not
  the engine; the engine's outputs agreed with product/order checks
  throughout.) mathx suites green.

## T-CODEQL-4 — ml bootstrap `% rows` — KEPT (loop win, macro-neutral)

- Rows CANNOT be rounded to a power of two (changes the sample). The
  multiply-high construction was validated EXACT first: `probe/fastmod_probe.c`
  ran 153.9M adversarial+random (n, d<2^32) checks. The from-memory Lemire
  lowbits variant FAILED it (128.5M mismatches, first n=2^64-1 d=3) and was
  rejected; the mulhi + conditional add-back form passed everything except
  d == 1 (M overflows), which the caller special-cases (rows==1 keeps taking
  the draws and maps to 0 — `probe/rows1_probe.js` behavior-identical to
  base).
- Helpers `dyn_fastmod_M`/`dyn_fastmod` live in `src/core/dyn-prng.h` (the
  module whose determinism contract covers ml sampling), exactness documented.
- Bootstrap draw loop is BIT-IDENTICAL: checksum over 100M draws matches
  (`probe/bench_draws.c`). Loop micro: 2.42 -> 2.31 ns/draw (-5..-16% of the
  loop; it is splitmix64-bound). JS-level: stump-heavy forest (10M draws)
  -0.85% (5/5 reps ordered); full forest fits -0.15..-0.2% (tree fit
  dominates). Chi-square over 1M draws (`probe/chi2_fastmod.c`): statistics
  IDENTICAL to division at rows 1000/997/65536/40000, all uniform within
  4sd of df.
- Fold assignment `(cnt % k) + 1` -> wrap counter (k validated [2, n];
  equal by induction). test_ml_selection 343 green (stratifiedKFold).
- Judgment: kept because the finding's loop itself measures faster with
  bit-identical output and proven exactness; macro numbers recorded honestly.

## T-CODEQL-5 — sel_part_t 31% padding — KEPT (footprint; perf neutral)

- 32 -> 24 bytes (a/b pointers first, sub+kind+op last; 2 tail bytes),
  `_Static_assert` pins the layout (house style, cf san_t). No behavior
  change: field access is by name; no serialization/memcmp of parts exists
  (verified by grep; html suites below).
- Correctness: test_html 108, test_html_text 9, test_html_large 24,
  test_html_pentest 25 green; match results identical (acc 134250/140000 on
  both binaries in every bench).
- Perf: match-heavy (6 compound selectors x 80k nodes) 48-52 ms both;
  parse-heavy 2.0 ms both; group-walk (1300 comma groups -> every node walks
  the whole parts array) medians quantize to 1677/1727/1799 ms on BOTH
  binaries — no reproducible delta. Reachable parts arrays are bounded by
  the 4096-byte selector-string cap (~1365 minimal groups); 41.6 KB vs
  31.2 KB are both L1-resident, so the cache benefit the finding projected
  is not observable at reachable scales. Kept as the briefed layout fix with
  its verification bar met (static_assert), zero risk, -25%/element.

